/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-83-  // 26-remove-duplicates). Cross-frame reads (a comprehension closure
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-84-  // reading the enclosing function's cellvar) deref inside #look instead.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-85-  rule <k> cellRef(H:Int) => V ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-86-       <env> L:Int </env>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-87-       <scopes> ... L |-> scope(M:Map, _) ... </scopes>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-88-       <heap> ... H |-> cellV(V:Val) ... </heap>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-89-       requires "$cells" in_keys(M)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-90-       [priority(40)]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-91-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-92-  // write through a cell (Assign / #bindP / #bindTgt dispatch here on
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-93-  // cell-bound names)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-94-  // a keyword argument cools to a TAGGED value (consumed by kw-aware builtins)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k:95:  syntax Val ::= kwV(String, Val)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-96-  syntax KItem ::= #kwTag(String)
